WEBVTT

00:01.020 --> 00:10.930
<i>I'm gonna go look for your smile, shining like the sun</i>

00:10.930 --> 00:20.000
<i>The waving flowers can't
 hide their feelings forever</i>

00:20.550 --> 00:32.510
<i>It's all right, I'll work up 
all my courage and tell you</i>

00:33.430 --> 00:35.600
<i>That I love you</i>

00:52.190 --> 00:54.860
<b>Hokkaido Gals Are Super Adorable!</b>

00:55.700 --> 00:59.070
<b>Hokkaido Gals Are Super Adorable!</b>

02:07.230 --> 02:09.980
Super Cute Angels ♥

02:07.230 --> 02:09.980
<b>Hokkaido Gals Are</b>

02:07.230 --> 02:09.980
<b>Boom!</b>

02:07.230 --> 02:09.980
<b>Super Adorable</b>

02:10.840 --> 02:13.490
Yay! Thanks!

02:10.850 --> 02:15.320
<b>Episode 5:
Super Bitter, Super Sweet</b>

02:10.850 --> 02:15.320
<b>Episode 5:
Super Bitter, Super Sweet</b>

02:14.860 --> 02:15.990
Standby...

02:16.580 --> 02:18.720
Fuyuki-san is such a good singer!

02:18.720 --> 02:21.500
Yeah. She's got serious party girl vibes.

02:21.500 --> 02:25.670
Fuyumina, you sing that 
every time we go to karaoke.

02:25.670 --> 02:28.480
Yeah, I love this song.

02:28.480 --> 02:30.500
It always cheers me up!

02:31.770 --> 02:33.260
By the way...

02:33.670 --> 02:35.690
Ah, sorry. What?

02:35.690 --> 02:39.280
Do you go to karaoke a lot, Shiki?

02:39.280 --> 02:43.190
No. I've only gone a few times with family.

02:43.190 --> 02:47.520
So I'm glad Fuyuki-san invited me 
today, but I'm pretty nervous.

02:47.520 --> 02:48.700
What about you?

02:49.440 --> 02:53.210
Well, yeah. By myself, anyway.

02:55.700 --> 02:58.330
Y-You mean you solo karaoke?!

02:58.330 --> 03:02.020
Hey, everyone has their own thing! 
I think it's really great!

03:02.020 --> 03:05.460
Shiki, you're so sincere, it almost hurts.

03:02.220 --> 03:05.460
<b>Loneliness</b>

03:02.720 --> 03:05.460
<b>Kind words</b>

03:03.220 --> 03:05.460
<b>Gloom</b>

03:05.460 --> 03:08.280
Come on, Shiki-kun. Put in a song!

03:08.280 --> 03:10.070
Akino-san, what will you sing?

03:09.270 --> 03:10.740
Hey, like this one?

03:10.740 --> 03:11.740
Um...

03:11.740 --> 03:13.680
What do you usually listen to?

03:12.110 --> 03:14.920
I don't actually know a 
lot of mainstream stuff.

03:13.680 --> 03:15.780
Well, um...

03:16.100 --> 03:18.110


03:18.110 --> 03:20.890
I'll look for songs with you!

03:20.890 --> 03:23.930
Huh? But you just sang, Fuyumina!

03:23.930 --> 03:27.820
I'm just helping Tsubasa and 
Sayurin find a song they can sing.

03:27.820 --> 03:29.150
Okay with you guys?

03:30.810 --> 03:31.650
<i>Yeah!</i>

03:31.650 --> 03:33.470
<i>Good job, Fuyuki-san!</i>

03:31.650 --> 03:33.470
<i>Good job, Fuyuki!</i>

03:33.470 --> 03:35.210
Fuyumina, you're up!

03:37.970 --> 03:39.380
Let's sing it together!

03:45.770 --> 03:49.240
Ugh. It's almost time for finals.

03:49.240 --> 03:53.600
The exams cover way too much 
stuff this time. Right, Shiki-kun?

03:53.600 --> 03:55.670
Uh, yeah. They sure do.

03:55.670 --> 03:58.480
Hey! Let's all have a study party, man!

03:58.480 --> 03:59.010
Oh!

03:59.010 --> 04:00.590
Aww, yeah! Let's do it!

04:00.590 --> 04:03.220
Your nails are so cute, Akino-san!

04:03.220 --> 04:06.270
Uh, thanks. I really like this color.

04:09.270 --> 04:10.450
<b>Recent</b>

04:09.270 --> 04:10.450
Select Multiple

04:10.450 --> 04:12.270
Chocolate

04:10.450 --> 04:12.270
Don't Miss!

04:10.450 --> 04:12.270
Perfect for
This Year's Valentine's!!

04:10.450 --> 04:12.270
Too Cute
Valentine Chocolate

04:12.270 --> 04:16.240
You know what? 
It's almost Valentine's Day.

04:19.320 --> 04:22.340
I simply have no interest in 
getting chocolates at all.

04:22.340 --> 04:23.740
I-I know, right?

04:24.010 --> 04:26.060
You sure don't sound like you mean it!

04:26.060 --> 04:28.370
I'll give you some courtesy 
chocolates if you want.

04:28.370 --> 04:30.900
Seriously? I'm glad I spoke up!

04:30.900 --> 04:31.950
Sweet!

04:32.870 --> 04:34.900
<i>Valentine's, huh?</i>

04:36.080 --> 04:39.400
<i>I wonder if Fuyuki-san is 
giving anyone chocolates.</i>

04:39.840 --> 04:43.260
Fuyumina! Gimme chocolates, okay?

04:43.260 --> 04:45.470
Huh? Sure!

04:47.430 --> 04:50.400
I'm gonna make a ton of chocolates this year!

04:50.400 --> 04:52.960
How many did you make last year?

04:54.040 --> 04:55.270
About 60, I think.

04:55.270 --> 04:58.120
Yeah, you passed them out like school lunch.

04:59.030 --> 05:03.520
<i>Oh, okay. Fuyuki-san gives 
everyone chocolates.</i>

05:03.520 --> 05:06.920
<i>Wait. Why do I feel so... relieved?</i>

05:08.840 --> 05:11.400
Do you like to make chocolates 
and stuff, Akino-san?

05:12.170 --> 05:16.130
No. I'd rather save that 
money for my hobbies.

05:16.130 --> 05:20.360
Hilarious! It's so cool that 
you say what you really think!

05:21.430 --> 05:23.310
<i>That does describe Akino-san.</i>

05:23.310 --> 05:26.460
Did you get chocolates from 
girls in Tokyo, Shiki-kun?

05:26.460 --> 05:28.330
Only from my family.

05:28.330 --> 05:29.810
Yeah, relatable.

05:29.810 --> 05:32.050
Oh, come on. That doesn't even count!

05:32.050 --> 05:35.320
So you're one of those, Shiki-kun? 
I never would have guessed!

05:36.650 --> 05:40.650
Wedding After-parties
Special Benefits for Newlyweds and Planners

05:37.140 --> 05:38.210
'Kay, let's call it!

05:38.210 --> 05:39.340
All right.

05:38.210 --> 05:39.340
Bye-bye!

05:39.340 --> 05:39.910
See you!

05:39.910 --> 05:40.650
Later!

05:40.900 --> 05:43.880
<i>I had so much fun talking to everyone today!</i>

05:43.880 --> 05:45.410
<i>I'm glad I came.</i>

05:45.910 --> 05:47.110
Tsubasa!

05:45.910 --> 05:47.110
Shiki!

05:48.660 --> 05:51.860
Uh, so, how was it? Did you have fun?

05:51.860 --> 05:53.560
Yeah, I had a good time.

05:53.560 --> 05:54.700
What about you, Sayurin?

05:54.700 --> 05:56.090
Me, too.

05:56.290 --> 06:00.090
Really? I'm so glad! 
I'll invite you again next time.

06:00.530 --> 06:01.280
Sure.

06:01.960 --> 06:05.380
Akino-san, what's up? 
Didn't you want to say something?

06:05.380 --> 06:08.640
Uh, no. Never mind. It's nothing.

06:10.550 --> 06:12.100
Should we get going, then?

06:12.100 --> 06:15.110
You're such a good singer, Tsubasa.

06:15.110 --> 06:17.060
Huh? You think so?

06:19.900 --> 06:22.400
Valentine's Special 
10 Questions to Find Out
What Kind of Chocolate He Likes 
Valentine's Day is coming up!
How to grab his heart and...

06:24.130 --> 06:25.640
Sayurin?

06:29.240 --> 06:31.120
Sorry!

06:46.260 --> 06:48.760
<b>Saturday, February 2</b>

06:50.180 --> 06:54.070
Forget about chocolate! 
The event is more important!

07:09.920 --> 07:11.190
Sayurin?

07:11.830 --> 07:12.630
Oh, my god!

07:12.630 --> 07:13.780
Yoo-hoo!

07:13.780 --> 07:15.690
F-Fuyuki?

07:15.690 --> 07:17.190
What are you doing here?

07:17.550 --> 07:19.960
I came to buy ingredients to make chocolates.

07:20.410 --> 07:23.280
Oh. Right. I see.

07:23.810 --> 07:26.280
Are you shopping for something, too?

07:26.280 --> 07:30.850
Um... nail polish? Mine is coming off.

07:30.850 --> 07:32.340
No, it's not.

07:32.870 --> 07:34.650
Wh-What? I guess you're right!

07:38.370 --> 07:40.150
Are you actually here to—

07:40.150 --> 07:43.000
Cosmetics! I came to buy cosmetics!

07:43.000 --> 07:45.950
Oh, right! You know a lot 
about cosmetics, don't you?

07:45.950 --> 07:48.280
Would you mind helping me pick things out?

07:52.170 --> 07:53.750
Thank you very much.

07:54.500 --> 07:57.920
When I see something good, 
I just can't help myself!

07:58.410 --> 08:01.170
I'll bring the ones we're sharing to school.

08:01.170 --> 08:02.870
Yeah. Thanks.

08:02.870 --> 08:07.800
Personally, I might be really into 
this limited Valentine's lipstick!

08:08.040 --> 08:12.680
Oh, speaking of Valentine's, what kind 
of chocolate do you like, Sayurin?

08:14.310 --> 08:15.960
Sayurin? What's wrong?

08:15.960 --> 08:19.400
Huh? I-I like ganache and stuff.

08:19.400 --> 08:21.190
Oh, I totally get that!

08:21.190 --> 08:25.320
Whenever I go to Sapporo, I always 
buy Royce's Nama Chocolate!

08:26.450 --> 08:28.370
I wanna go to Sapporo!

08:28.370 --> 08:31.990
Oh, oops! I gotta go buy those ingredients.

08:31.990 --> 08:33.470
Oh.

08:33.780 --> 08:35.490
M'kay, see you later!

08:40.420 --> 08:41.300
Uh...

08:42.740 --> 08:45.690
Maybe I can... shop with you?

08:47.670 --> 08:52.420
Hey, don't get me wrong! You know why! 
I wanna make chocolates for you!

08:55.780 --> 08:58.980
I'm gonna make you super delish 
chocolates, Sayurin! The best!

08:59.300 --> 09:01.190
Yes! Here we go!

09:01.190 --> 09:03.560
Hey, quit running!

09:06.070 --> 09:09.660
If you need help with the 
chocolates, call me anytime.

09:09.660 --> 09:11.360
Okay. Thanks.

09:11.360 --> 09:12.540
See you later!

09:16.210 --> 09:17.220
Fuyuki.

09:18.840 --> 09:20.040
Don't you want...

09:24.080 --> 09:27.160
to give Shiki the real thing instead? 
Special chocolates?

09:36.400 --> 09:38.890
Uh, b-but why Tsubasa?

09:38.890 --> 09:41.290
I mean, you two get along so well...

09:41.620 --> 09:43.650
Well, yeah. We're friends!

09:43.650 --> 09:46.080
Aren't you buddy-buddy with him, too?

09:46.080 --> 09:48.900
Yeah, but we just play games together.

09:53.340 --> 09:55.530
Uh, sorry. That came out of nowhere.

09:55.530 --> 09:59.260
No, it's okay. It just surprised me a little.

09:59.420 --> 10:01.040
Okay, see you at school.

10:01.040 --> 10:02.750
Yeah. See you.

10:15.610 --> 10:17.300
<i>But which is it?</i>

10:26.190 --> 10:28.070
<b>Midnight Sunflower</b>

10:31.150 --> 10:34.320
I think I've basically 
covered the exam material.

10:35.130 --> 10:36.570
<b>Sunday, February 13</b>

10:35.130 --> 10:36.570
<b>Midnight Sunflower</b>

10:37.430 --> 10:40.250
<i>I sh-shouldn't get my hopes up about tomorrow!</i>

10:40.250 --> 10:43.060
<i>With finals so close, it isn't 
the time for that anyway.</i>

10:42.620 --> 10:46.000
<b>Midnight Sunflower</b>

10:43.430 --> 10:44.770
<i>Study, study!</i>

10:52.010 --> 10:54.010
<b>Fuyuki</b>

10:52.010 --> 10:54.010
<b>I guess we bought a lot of different lipstick
and nail polish to share, huh?</b>

10:52.010 --> 10:54.010
<b>Thanks for going shopping with me!</b>

10:52.010 --> 10:54.010
<b>I guess we did promise to go</b>

10:56.800 --> 10:58.900
<b><i><i>Sayurin, you still awake?</i></i></b>

10:56.800 --> 11:03.730
<b>Sayurin, you still awake?</b>

10:58.900 --> 11:03.720
<b><i><i>I'm almost done making chocolates, and
I started to wonder how you were doing.</i></i></b>

11:07.120 --> 11:08.690
Oh, it's Sayurin!

11:08.960 --> 11:11.670
<b><i>I always play games around 
this time, so I'm still awake.</i></b>

11:12.020 --> 11:13.780
<b><i>I'm about to start the chocolates.</i></b>

11:16.780 --> 11:18.940
<i>Sorry to bother you!</i>

11:18.940 --> 11:22.510
<i>We've never talked on the phone 
before, so this is kinda exciting!</i>

11:23.760 --> 11:25.340
Well that's beside the point.

11:25.340 --> 11:26.330
<i>I'm beside the point?!</i>

11:26.330 --> 11:28.970
<i>What's the best way to make chocolates?</i>

11:28.970 --> 11:31.530
<i>I'd rather make a type that isn't too hard.</i>

11:32.310 --> 11:34.300
I know exactly what to do!

11:34.300 --> 11:37.520
<i>First, take a knife and chop 
the chocolate into little bits.</i>

11:37.520 --> 11:38.970
Roger.

11:39.480 --> 11:41.970
<b>Mad rhythm and button-mashing
skills developed by gaming</b>

11:41.970 --> 11:43.650
<i>Done. What's next.</i>

11:43.650 --> 11:44.980
Already?

11:44.980 --> 11:50.450
Got that fresh cream you bought today? 
Put that in a bowl and double boil it.

11:50.450 --> 11:51.440
Double boil?

11:51.440 --> 11:53.900
Double boiling is when 
you heat water in a pot

11:51.440 --> 11:54.620
<b><i></i>Heat up water</b>

11:53.900 --> 11:56.610
and you put another container with your 
ingredient inside that to warm it up.

11:54.670 --> 11:57.780
<b><i></i>Ingredient you
want to heat</b>

11:56.170 --> 11:57.780
<b><i></i>Don't let the hot
water get inside!!</b>

11:56.610 --> 11:57.780
<i>Oh, I get it.</i>

11:58.320 --> 12:01.280
<i>Use half as much cream as chocolate.</i>

12:01.280 --> 12:02.810
So about this much?

12:03.300 --> 12:05.240
<b>Guesstimating candy ingredients is absolutely prohibited</b>

12:05.250 --> 12:10.210
<i>Turn off the flame, put in the chopped 
chocolate, then stir and stir as it melts.</i>

12:10.570 --> 12:15.820
<i>Cool it for one or two hours in the fridge 
and then cut it into any size you want.</i>

12:15.820 --> 12:17.880
Then all that's left is the cocoa powder!

12:18.180 --> 12:22.760
That really was easy. 
How are your chocolates looking, Fuyuki?

12:22.760 --> 12:25.310
Mine? Well...

12:27.180 --> 12:29.770
You'll just have to wait until tomorrow!

12:29.990 --> 12:31.800
<i>How many pieces did you end up making?</i>

12:31.800 --> 12:34.500
Seventy! A new record for me!

12:34.500 --> 12:37.290
<i>You've got so many friends, it's scary!</i>

12:37.290 --> 12:39.530
<i>I'm surprised you can 
keep yourself motivated.</i>

12:37.290 --> 12:42.780
Mitsuba Milk

12:39.530 --> 12:41.930
Well, it makes everyone really happy.

12:41.930 --> 12:46.460
And I start wondering, "How are they 
gonna react to this one?" and stuff.

12:46.460 --> 12:48.410
I get excited just thinking about it!

12:49.250 --> 12:52.040
I know I'm the one having 
the most fun, though.

12:52.920 --> 12:56.280
<i>Who were you thinking of when you made yours?</i>

12:56.880 --> 13:01.460
I... I told you it's for you! Don't make 
me say it out loud. It's embarrassing.

13:01.460 --> 13:03.550
<i>Squee! I'm so happy!</i>

13:06.080 --> 13:07.060
But who else?

13:07.980 --> 13:09.910
<i>Are you giving some to anyone else?</i>

13:11.620 --> 13:13.980
I've actually been wondering for a while.

13:14.820 --> 13:19.660
<i>About you and Tsubasa. Do you maybe...</i>

13:21.430 --> 13:21.780
li—

13:22.740 --> 13:23.570
Huh?

13:25.280 --> 13:28.380
<i>No! Stop!</i>

13:28.380 --> 13:30.460
H-Hey, what's wrong? You okay?

13:30.700 --> 13:33.210
<i>What happened? Fuyuki!</i>

13:33.680 --> 13:38.210
I just spilled condiments and a bottle 
of soy sauce on my chocolates.

13:38.210 --> 13:40.630
Huh?! And the chocolates? Are they okay?

13:40.630 --> 13:43.690
No, they're drenched in soy sauce.

13:43.690 --> 13:45.200
<i>You mean all of them?</i>

13:45.200 --> 13:46.700
Yep, all.

13:47.560 --> 13:49.060
F-Fuyuki...

13:49.060 --> 13:53.410
<i>But hey, it's my fault for 
not cleaning up first.</i>

13:53.730 --> 13:58.270
<i>Is your ganache going to be okay? You still 
remember the instructions I gave you?</i>

13:58.270 --> 14:00.780
Uh, yeah. I do.

14:00.780 --> 14:05.190
Oh, good. M'kay, I gotta clean 
up so I'll catch you later.

14:00.780 --> 14:06.030
<b>Fuyuki Minami 
In Call</b>

14:05.190 --> 14:06.530
H-Hey!

14:06.030 --> 14:06.530
<b>I'm about to start making chocolate</b>

14:06.030 --> 14:06.530
<b>The phone call has ended</b>

14:08.870 --> 14:11.620
<b>The phone call has ended</b>

14:09.430 --> 14:11.070
<b><i>Good luck, Sayurin!</i></b>

14:13.080 --> 14:15.250
How can you be so nice right now?

14:22.840 --> 14:28.650
<i>Ugh. I was up so late studying 
last night. Didn't sleep at all.</i>

14:31.600 --> 14:34.440
<i>Well, anyway. So...</i>

14:36.600 --> 14:38.560
<i>Bring it!</i>

14:40.360 --> 14:41.650
<i>Yes, of course I got nothing!</i>

14:45.190 --> 14:47.320
Tsubasa, good morning!

14:49.160 --> 14:51.230
G-Good morning, Fuyuki-san.

14:51.880 --> 14:52.830
<i>What?</i>

14:53.220 --> 14:56.330
<i>Fuyuki-san's eyes look kind of red.</i>

14:56.330 --> 14:58.630
Here, Tsubasa! This is for you.

14:58.630 --> 14:59.170
Huh?

15:00.060 --> 15:01.250
<i>No way.</i>

15:01.690 --> 15:03.300
<b>White Black
Thunder</b>

15:02.410 --> 15:03.300
What's this?

15:03.300 --> 15:06.640
Because it's Valentine's Day. 
These are really good!

15:06.640 --> 15:08.580
I bet you can't find them in Tokyo.

15:09.200 --> 15:12.430
Thank you, Fuyuki-san! I promise to enjoy it!

15:17.630 --> 15:19.700
Ah! Good morning, Sayurin!

15:19.700 --> 15:21.070
Something for you.

15:22.120 --> 15:23.240
This...?

15:27.890 --> 15:30.470
Fuyumina! Give me a chocolate, too!

15:30.470 --> 15:31.740
Okay, okay!

15:31.740 --> 15:33.200
<b>White Black
Thunder</b>

15:32.230 --> 15:34.820
Huh? It isn't homemade?

15:34.820 --> 15:38.270
Production this year was suspended 
due to unforeseen circumstances.

15:38.270 --> 15:40.650
Aww man. I was looking forward to it.

15:40.650 --> 15:44.260
Well, sorry! Just take it 
and, like, don't complain!

15:44.740 --> 15:47.840
What a total letdown.

15:49.090 --> 15:50.740
Mat-sun!

15:52.050 --> 15:53.560
What's up?

15:53.880 --> 15:56.690
<i>So she didn't make chocolates this year?</i>

15:56.690 --> 15:57.980
<i>I wonder if something happened.</i>

15:58.450 --> 16:00.400
Thank ya. Later!

16:02.230 --> 16:02.770
Yo.

16:03.600 --> 16:06.190
Next time you talk to Fuyuki like that,

16:06.650 --> 16:08.260
I'm literally gonna pound you.

16:15.580 --> 16:18.080
Exam Range

16:15.580 --> 16:18.080


16:27.200 --> 16:30.510
Starting today, 
clubs are on hiatus for exams.

16:30.510 --> 16:34.010
Be sure to head straight home 
unless you have cleaning duties.

16:35.220 --> 16:37.230
<b>Cleaning Assignments</b>

16:35.220 --> 16:37.230
<b>Group 1</b>

16:35.220 --> 16:37.230
<b>Off</b>

16:35.220 --> 16:37.230
<b>Group 2</b>

16:35.220 --> 16:37.230
<b>Music Room</b>

16:35.220 --> 16:37.230
<b>Group 3</b>

16:35.220 --> 16:37.230
<b>Hallway</b>

16:35.220 --> 16:37.230
<b>Group 4</b>

16:35.220 --> 16:37.230
<b>Classroom</b>

16:40.100 --> 16:42.360
<b>Good luck, Sayurin</b>

16:45.110 --> 16:48.110
<b>Music Room</b>

16:45.550 --> 16:48.110
All that's left is taking out the trash.

16:48.390 --> 16:51.120
M'kay, you guys can handle the rest.

16:53.350 --> 16:57.590
You know, we always hear the 
band practicing after class,

16:57.590 --> 17:01.080
so it feels kinda weird when 
the school is this quiet.

17:01.080 --> 17:04.180
You're right. It feels like 
we're the only ones here.

17:05.620 --> 17:09.300
S-So anyway, thanks for the chocolate!

17:09.300 --> 17:11.320
I'll eat it when I get home.

17:13.520 --> 17:14.470
Fuyuki-san?

17:16.220 --> 17:17.140
Huh?

17:29.420 --> 17:30.460
Fuyuki-san!

17:31.860 --> 17:33.340
If it's okay with you,

17:33.840 --> 17:36.120
would you please tell me what happened?

17:40.260 --> 17:42.050
Oh, so that's it.

17:42.480 --> 17:45.870
All of the chocolates you made got ruined.

17:45.870 --> 17:49.630
I still thought that some 
of them would be okay.

17:49.630 --> 17:53.400
They were just cracked or 
got a little milk on them.

17:53.940 --> 17:57.760
But who'd want to give someone 
chocolates that were messed up?

17:58.990 --> 18:01.200
But still, even then,

18:01.830 --> 18:04.310
I really wanted to give everyone 
the chocolates I made.

18:06.380 --> 18:08.650
I feel like I disappointed everyone!

18:12.230 --> 18:15.130
I wanted you to have some, too, Tsubasa.

18:22.280 --> 18:27.560
Anyway, Mom told me to clean 
up first and I didn't listen.

18:27.560 --> 18:31.970
And then I asked something weird on 
the phone that bothered my friend.

18:32.530 --> 18:36.200
I was acting so thoughtless and 
now I'm being punished for it.

18:44.290 --> 18:45.520
Tsubasa?

18:52.310 --> 18:53.150
<i>Right now</i>

18:54.900 --> 18:56.810
<i>this is all I can do for her.</i>

19:49.330 --> 19:50.620
Was that...?

19:50.620 --> 19:53.630
Yeah. It's the song you sang at karaoke.

19:54.400 --> 19:58.800
I've studied piano so I thought 
I could try to learn it by ear.

19:58.800 --> 19:59.640
How was it?

19:59.930 --> 20:02.950
Huh?! Insane! You totally nailed it!

20:03.350 --> 20:05.930
But why this song?

20:05.930 --> 20:12.100
You always cheer me up, Fuyuki-san, 
so I wanted to cheer you up this time.

20:14.350 --> 20:16.360
Yeah, I love this song.

20:16.740 --> 20:18.450
It always cheers me up!

20:21.490 --> 20:25.250
Why do you always do stuff 
like this, Tsubasa? Seriously.

20:26.440 --> 20:28.750
I'm super cheered up now!

20:28.750 --> 20:32.180
You're the best. My happiness is maxed out!

20:32.180 --> 20:34.330
You stud, Tsuba-cha!

20:34.330 --> 20:35.600
<i>I'm glad.</i>

20:37.150 --> 20:38.260
Akino-san?

20:37.150 --> 20:38.260
Sayurin?

20:38.730 --> 20:40.100
What are you doing here?

20:40.520 --> 20:42.660
Well, you know.

20:43.020 --> 20:44.880
I've got chocolates to give away.

20:44.880 --> 20:45.270
Huh?

20:48.440 --> 20:51.810
Gotcha. 'Kay, I'd better go, then.

20:53.110 --> 20:54.020
To Fuyuki.

20:54.460 --> 20:55.440
Huh?!

20:56.850 --> 21:00.070
Oh, man. You don't remember? 
I promised. Buddy chocos.

21:00.400 --> 21:02.840
Buddy chocos?

21:03.830 --> 21:06.660
Sayurin! Love you!

21:06.660 --> 21:09.070
Hey, watch it! Your nose is running!

21:09.070 --> 21:11.020
Hey, can I open it?

21:11.020 --> 21:12.940
I guess. But you're gonna eat them now?

21:12.940 --> 21:15.090
Yeah, right now!

21:15.090 --> 21:15.850
But this is so—

21:15.850 --> 21:20.550
<i>Embarrassing! It was so obvious 
I thought they were for me!</i>

21:20.880 --> 21:24.550
<i>I want to dig a hole! 
I want to burrow deep into the earth!</i>

21:25.180 --> 21:28.020
Shiki. Here are yours.

21:29.380 --> 21:31.000
Huh? You had some for me?

21:31.000 --> 21:33.240
Might, as well. You are my disciple.

21:33.240 --> 21:35.820
When I made chocolates for Fuyuki, 
I had some left over.

21:37.730 --> 21:39.940
Thank you, Akino-san!

21:41.720 --> 21:44.540
You were really cool on the piano just now.

21:49.200 --> 21:53.490
Yum! Sayurin, these are super delish!

21:53.490 --> 21:55.900
For real? Even though it was my first time?

21:55.900 --> 21:59.110
Ooh! And Tsubasa got some, too?

21:59.110 --> 22:01.010
They're buddy chocos, just like yours.

22:01.010 --> 22:04.090
Let's all eat them together!

22:04.720 --> 22:05.700
Yeah!

22:05.700 --> 22:08.580
I've got the chocolate you gave 
me in my pocket, Fuyuki-san.

22:08.580 --> 22:10.680
Can I go ahead and eat it?

22:11.140 --> 22:13.100
I've got mine in my bag.

22:13.100 --> 22:17.110
Nice, nice! It's choco-party time! 
Choco-party!
